//! Asymmetric keys for the crypto bridge over silk.crypto: RSA, EC (P-256, P-384, P-521,
//! secp256k1, P-224, P-192), Ed25519 and X25519. A key is kept as compact data (RSA as its PKCS #1
//! DER; EC as its curve, scalar and uncompressed point; Ed25519 and X25519 as seed and public
//! bytes). Import and export take PEM and DER: SubjectPublicKeyInfo, PKCS #8 (plain and PBES2
//! encrypted), PKCS #1, SEC1 and legacy encrypted PEM. Signatures are RSA PKCS #1 v1.5 and PSS,
//! ECDSA (DER) and Ed25519; key agreement is ECDH and X25519; encryption is RSA OAEP, PKCS #1 v1.5
//! and raw. Failures carry OpenSSL's error strings, as ../openssl's bridge reports them.
